  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe core idea is to reframe the problem as maximizing the minimum autocorrelation integral \u222b h(x)h(x+k)dx over all shifts k, which equates to minimizing the maximum overlap integral C\u2085. This reformulation allows us to focus on designing h that maintains uniform overlap across shifts, avoiding local minima that previous methods failed to escape. The strategy uses a dynamic initialization with evenly spaced binary events, optimized using a convex relaxation with log-sum-exp surrogates to approximate the max operation. This enables efficient gradient-based optimization and structured perturbations to escape poor local optima.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\nRepresentation: \n- h_flat (n_points-length vector) with 0 \u2264 h_flat[i] \u2264 1\n- Target sum: target_sum = n_points / 2\n- dx = 2.0 / n_points\n- Autocorrelation integral for shift k: ac_k = \u222b h(x)h(x+k)dx \u2248 np.correlate(h, h, mode='full')[k] * dx\n- Objective: minimize C\u2085 = 1 - max_k ac_k \u2192 maximize min_k ac_k\n\nConstraints:\n- 0 \u2264 h_flat[i] \u2264 1\n- \u2211h_flat = target_sum\n\nSurrogate: C\u2085_approx = (1/\u03b1) * ln(\u03a3 exp(\u03b1 * (1 - ac_k))) for \u03b1=1000\n\nOptimization:\n- SLSQP with bounds [0,1] and equality constraint \u2211h_flat = target_sum\n- Post-optimization validation with exact objective\n\n3. Implementation procedure\nParent validation:\n- If initial_h_values is provided, use it\n- Else: Generate binary pattern with m = n_points//2 evenly spaced 1's in [0, 2], scaled to meet \u2211h_flat = target_sum\n\nInitialization:\n- Compute even spacing s = 2 / m\n- Set h_flat[i] = 1 if i*s \u2264 2 and i = 0, m, 2m, ..., m\u00b2\n\nOptimization loop:\n- Stage 1 (Surrogate-based):\n   - Use log-sum-exp surrogate with \u03b1=1000\n   - Run SLSQP with maxiter=200 and tolerance=1e-8\n   - Apply structured perturbations: swap 0/1 at positions with high ac_k every 5 iterations\n- Stage 2 (Exact-based):\n   - Switch to exact objective evaluation\n   - Run L-BFGS-B with maxiter=50\n   - Apply Gaussian noise (\u03c3=0.02) every 10 iterations, then clamp and rescale\n\nCandidate acceptance:\n- Track best solution (highest min ac_k)\n- Validate \u2211h_flat \u2248 target_sum (tolerance 1e-6)\n- Ensure all h_flat[i] \u2208 [0,1]\n\nTermination:\n- Stop when time budget exhausted or no improvement in 10 iterations\n- Return best solution and its C\u2085 bound\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\nDefault configuration:\n- n_points=200\n- Stage 1: SLSQP with \u03b1=1000, 200 iterations, structured perturbations\n- Stage 2: L-BFGS-B with 50 iterations, Gaussian noise every 10 iterations\n- Perturbations: swap 0/1 at positions with high ac_k (determined via min ac_k index)\n\nVariations:\n- Binary initialization with denser/further spacing (m = n_points//3 to m = n_points//2)\n- Surrogate \u03b1 values: 500, 1000, 2000\n- Solver combinations: SLSQP + L-BFGS-B\n- Noise patterns: uniform, Gaussian, Cauchy\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\nTime allocation:\n- Stage 1: 200 iterations with SLSQP (each iteration ~1s) = ~200s\n- Stage 2: 50 iterations with L-BFGS-B (each iteration ~1s) = ~50s\n- Perturbations: 100s\n- Final refinement: 150s\n\nRobustness:\n- For nan values: clamp to [0,1], rescale\n- For constraint violation: project to feasible region by adjusting values\n- Fallback: use initial_h_values if all optimizations fail\n- Early exit: if no improvement for 10 iterations\n\n6. Validation and return contract\nFeasibility checks:\n- \u2211h_flat \u2248 target_sum (tolerance 1e-6)\n- All h_flat[i] \u2208 [0,1]\n- C\u2085 bound is finite and matches exact evaluator\n\nFinal validation:\n- Re-evaluate candidate with exact objective\n- Compare with current best\n- Return (h_values, c5_bound, n_points) with n_points=200",
